.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-auth-status - Show the current authentication status


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 auth status [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Report whether this gateway has a usable session, and where it is stored.

.PP
Sessions are per gateway, in a file named after a digest of the base URL, so
\&'token_path' is the only way to know which file backs the current session —
useful when several environments are in play, or to remove one by hand.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-auth(1)\fP
